          "citation": "489 U.S. 189 (1989)",
          "court": "Supreme Court of the United States",
          "year": 1989,
          "date_decided": "1989-02-22",
          "holding": "The Court held that a State's failure to protect a child from private violence, even after the agency received repeated reports and took no action, does not violate the Due Process Clause, because the Clause imposes no affirmative duty of protection absent a custodial relationship.",
          "relevance": "Failure to meet child-welfare performance expectations is addressed through funding and administrative remedies, not a § 1983 due-process claim.",
